.TH mnnn-rule-edit 1  "mnnn-rule-edit 2.16.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-rule\-edit \- Change a rule: given \-\-on, \-\-if or \-\-then replace the old ones
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn rule edit\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-if\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-then\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-cron\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-if\fR] [\fB\-\-journal\fR] [\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-standalone\fR] [\fB\-\-related\fR] [\fB\-\-unrelated\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-schedule\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIRULE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a rule: given \-\-on, \-\-if or \-\-then replace the old ones
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Action kinds to react to: import, journal.*, * (repeat or comma\-separate)
.TP
\fB\-\-if\fR \fI<CONDITION>\fR
A condition: FIELD OP VALUE, e.g. "inserted > 0" (repeat: all must hold)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-then\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
A then\-action, e.g. "status Imported {inserted} bars" (repeat: run in order)
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR
Run it on a schedule: every 30m, 6h, 1d, 1w (the node runs it; see `mnnn rule tick`)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cron\fR \fI<CRON>\fR
Run it at cron times, local time: "0 3 * * *" (minute hour day month weekday)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-if\fR
Drop every condition
.TP
\fB\-\-journal\fR \fI<JOURNAL>\fR
Move it into a journal
.TP
\fB\-\-search\fR \fI<SEARCH>\fR
Move it into a live search
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Move it into a model
.TP
\fB\-\-standalone\fR
Take it out of its journal or live search (projects are kept)
.TP
\fB\-\-related\fR
Only react to actions about where it lives
.TP
\fB\-\-unrelated\fR
React to every matching action
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-schedule\fR
Stop running it on a schedule
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIRULE\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.16.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
